# Settings for the Bona Fide App. On the server, copy this file to /opt/bona-fide/.env, fill it
# in, and run `chmod 600 .env`. Never commit the filled-in copy.
#
# One value per line. Docker Compose expands `$` and cuts a value at ` #`, so wrap any value that
# contains `$`, `#` or a space in single quotes. Leave an optional line commented out to get its
# default: an empty value is not the default.

# --- Required ---

# The webhook secret set in the GitHub App's settings. Make one with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The GitHub App's App ID, the number on its settings page.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
# The GitHub App's private key (.pem) on one line, in single quotes, each line break written as \n.
GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY=
# An Arc RPC endpoint that serves historical state, such as https://rpc.mainnet.arc.io.
RPC_URL=
# The Bona Fide escrow's address on Arc.
ESCROW_ADDRESS=
# The block the escrow was deployed in. The App never looks at earlier blocks. Default: 0.
ESCROW_FROM_BLOCK=
# The deposit page. A check links to it with ?repo=owner/repo&kind=pr|issue&number=N.
DEPOSIT_PAGE_URL=
# The Maintainer's setup page, where they prove control of their wallet. Until a repo is set up, its
# checks link Maintainers to it with ?repo=owner/repo.
SETUP_PAGE_URL=

# --- Behind Caddy ---

# 1 makes the per-IP rate limits count each client by the rightmost X-Forwarded-For address,
# which Caddy sets to the client's real address. Keep it at 1 while Caddy is the only way to
# reach the App, as docker-compose.yml arranges; unset, every client shares Caddy's address.
TRUST_PROXY=1

# --- Optional ---

# How often the watcher checks the escrow for new Deposits, in milliseconds.
# POLL_MS=1000
# The block the watcher starts from after a restart. Default: 10,000 blocks before the latest,
# about 85 minutes on Arc. Set it after a longer outage, then comment it out again.
# WATCH_FROM_BLOCK=
# The App's port inside the container. docker-compose.yml sets it to 3000, so leave it unset.
# PORT=3000
# The block explorer a check links each Deposit's transaction to. Default: Arc mainnet's. On Arc
# testnet, set https://explorer.testnet.arc.io.
# EXPLORER_URL=https://explorer.arc.io
# The decision log's JSONL file, which GET /decisions serves for public repos. docker-compose.yml
# sets it to /data/decisions.jsonl on the bona-fide-data volume, so leave it unset. Default:
# data/decisions.jsonl in the App's working directory.
# DECISIONS_PATH=data/decisions.jsonl
# The JSONL file that links each Deposit to its Contributor for Record Exemptions, so a restart
# doesn't look them all up on GitHub again. docker-compose.yml sets it to /data/records.jsonl on the
# bona-fide-data volume, so leave it unset. Default: data/records.jsonl in the App's working directory.
# RECORDS_PATH=data/records.jsonl

# --- Keeper and deposit relay (optional) ---
# Arc gas is paid in USDC, so the address of each key needs a little USDC to send transactions.

# The private key of the escrow's Keeper address. It refunds Deposits, including every one past its
# Timeout, relays signed Forfeits (POST /forfeit) and binds repos (POST /binding-proof). Without it,
# the App runs its checks only.
# KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The Maintainer's sign page, linked with the same query as the deposit page. Required with the
# Keeper's key.
# SIGN_PAGE_URL=
# How often the Keeper looks for Bindings to activate, in milliseconds.
# ACTIVATE_MS=30000
# How often the Keeper looks for Deposits past their Timeout to refund, in milliseconds.
# REFUND_MS=30000
# The key that submits one-signature Deposits sent to POST /relay/deposit and pays their gas. It may
# be the Keeper's key. Without it, /relay/deposit answers 404.
# RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Triage and Record Exemptions (optional) ---
# Triage sends the title, body, changed files and diff of each PR or issue that holds a Deposit to
# Anthropic's API, and posts the model's suggestion for the Maintainer. It needs the Keeper's key.
# Record Exemptions send the counts of a Contributor's Bona Fide record and public GitHub profile,
# and their login, when their record reaches a repo's threshold.

# An Anthropic API key. Without it, triage and Record Exemptions are off.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The Claude model triage and Record Exemptions ask. Default: claude-opus-5.
# TRIAGE_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# --- Bounties (optional) ---
# The Keeper pays a Bounty from the Maintainer's Bounty wallet when a PR that closes its issue is
# merged, within the wallet's limits, and relays the Payouts Maintainers sign (POST /bounty/payout).
# It needs the Keeper's key. Without ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, every Bounty waits for the Maintainer's
# signature: only the model can confirm a PR resolves its issue.

# The BountyWalletFactory's address on Arc. Without it, Bounties are off.
# BOUNTY_FACTORY_ADDRESS=
# The block the factory was deployed in. The App looks for Payouts from there on. Default: 0.
# BOUNTY_FACTORY_FROM_BLOCK=
# The Bounty page, where a Maintainer signs a Payout. Notes link to it with
# ?repo=owner/repo&issue=N&payee=0x…. Required with the factory.
# BOUNTY_PAGE_URL=
